{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793806031,"nonce":"BUAEiNDaN2aMLUnnZsw/lab8u0o=","title":"Tiering: static-hot method_call requests LLVM that cannot finish before exit","message":"On commit dfc3eda54f4e8907cb33e0fc1cd3c6de9f5129b2, NUC zylua binary SHA256 6d1f60391c4e42bdb722845d4d3773a67b31f0df205d65dea39d8fbeeaa905ea: three diagnostic runs each at 100,000 and 1,000,000 iterations with LLVM enabled all request whole-chunk LLVM promotion after baseline compilation, but none publishes an entry or OSR helper, completes LLVM install, or performs an OSR transfer before process exit. Six corresponding Cranelift-only controls request no LLVM promotion. All twelve outputs are correct and all twelve place 119 native snapshot functions.\n\nThe ordinary ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE flag accidentally disables portable snapshot loading (separately tracked), so representative confirmation uses a scratch LD_PRELOAD getenv shim that returns 1 for that lookup without adding the variable to environ. Snapshot eligibility enumerates environ; all other getenv lookups pass through. This keeps the original binary and native snapshot while enabling actual transfer hooks. Diagnostic times are not benchmark results. Scripts, shim source and raw logs: /private/tmp/zyntax-method-tiers/evidence.tar.gz, SHA256 db9d77783705ad23b02cd219cf843b5050d904a460097ec33788fb6e53332057.\n\nExecution: lua$main is interpreted; lua$chunk is classified static-hot and its first call waits for optimized HIR plus Cranelift code. Toggle.activate, Toggle.value and NthToggle.activate are inlined into its loops. NthToggle.new is the sole remaining direct user-function call in optimized chunk HIR; constructors/helpers mix interpreter and Cranelift according to worker readiness. Library helpers normally use the native snapshot. The count of compiled bodies is not a count of executed calls.\n\nCause to address: tiered_backend.rs compile_lazy_function calls promote_static_hot immediately after publishing the baseline for a static-hot bead. loop_facts::STATIC_HOT_TRIPS is 4096; both loops have known 100,000 trips. promote_static_hot requests LLVM based on trip count without demonstrating enough remaining execution time to repay compilation. The first-call static-hot wait also dominates short-run latency: roughly 10 ms optimized-body preparation and 2-3 ms Cranelift emission in traced NUC runs; overlap means these are not additive wall-time buckets.\n\nPreviously collected uninstrumented paired medians: short wall ~30 ms in either configuration; long wall 49.665 ms LLVM enabled versus 46.164 ms Cranelift only. These mode labels indicate configuration, not proof of LLVM execution. Implement a promotion profitability/remaining-work policy and avoid speculative callee compilation that cannot serve another call. Preserve interpreter-first entry and OSR for genuinely long-lived loops. Related broader method_call issue: 53de3273d900a43d6ba866646d99875e82972744471affd0c481d6bc1ebd90bf.","files":null}]}